Hi Jonathan,

thanks for your interest and suggestion. I am familiar with ways to do this is STAN and JAGS; the issue is one of computational time, as INLA allows me to run the same model in a matter or 5 minutes at worst even with a large number of covariates, whilst it can take several hours to do the same in STAN/JAGS.

I appreciate the suggestion though, I may revert to that if no other solution can be found.

Incidentally another thought I had is: can a similar constraint over choice be approximated using priors?

Thanks,
R

