...however, in some cases the constraint itself isn’t really the point, but rather to only look at wellconstrained aspects of a nearly underdetermined model. In such cases, calculating contrasts etc from the posterior samples is a sensible thing to do. It’s not clear to me if that is the case for your model setting or not.

Finn

